WEBVTT

00:00:00.423 --> 00:00:03.463
Journey fifteen: run a business listing.

00:00:03.463 --> 00:00:08.859
An owner monitors the listing, edits its details, and pauses or resumes

00:00:08.859 --> 00:00:13.647
it. This run takes the journey from ninety percent to complete.

00:00:14.505 --> 00:00:19.574
Naomi owns Luzandre.com. On My business, Saved by members now carries

00:00:19.574 --> 00:00:24.275
its weekly change: twenty-eight members, four of them this week.

00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:29.417
The change counts the members who first saved the business in the last

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:30.225
seven days.

00:00:30.927 --> 00:00:36.351
Naomi has more than one business. A select named Business lists each one

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:41.776
with its stage. She chooses Laurent Photography, and the workspace moves

00:00:41.776 --> 00:00:45.015
to it: we're reviewing Laurent Photography.

00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:51.139
The choice is kept on the server, on the listing, so every page of the

00:00:51.139 --> 00:00:55.167
workspace follows it. She goes back to Luzandre.com.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:58.653
List another business opens the listing form.

00:00:59.355 --> 00:01:04.226
In the listing editor, photos are now reordered by dragging a handle.

00:01:04.226 --> 00:01:08.955
Naomi drags the third photo to the front, and it becomes the cover.

00:01:09.658 --> 00:01:15.196
The handle is for a pointer. With the keyboard, the move buttons do the

00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:17.458
same: move photo two earlier.

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:20.886
She changes the name of her live listing.

00:01:20.886 --> 00:01:25.671
The change is live at once, and the page says the verification team will

00:01:25.671 --> 00:01:28.529
take another look within two business days.

00:01:29.559 --> 00:01:34.691
New in this run, somebody is told. The verification team gets an e-mail

00:01:34.691 --> 00:01:39.100
with the old and the new name, and Naomi gets an e-mail and a

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.135
notification: we'll re-check her business.

00:01:43.166 --> 00:01:48.302
Members now see the photos. On the public page of a business, the cover

00:01:48.302 --> 00:01:53.366
stands in place of the tile, and the other photos follow under Photos.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.523
Each photo is a picture, with a WebP source and a JPEG fallback, a

00:01:58.523 --> 00:02:02.959
source set at the true widths, and its width and height, so the browser

00:02:02.959 --> 00:02:06.520
chooses a size for the screen and the page does not jump.

00:02:07.503 --> 00:02:12.733
Last, the pause. Naomi pauses her listing, and My business says it is

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:16.599
hidden from browse and search until she resumes it.

00:02:17.647 --> 00:02:22.145
The requirement says a paused listing leaves all public lists within

00:02:22.145 --> 00:02:26.709
sixty seconds. A new test proves it: on the welcome page, browse, the

00:02:26.709 --> 00:02:31.471
category, search and related businesses, and on what a browser may keep.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:38.019
Journey fifteen is complete. Left for the owner: the sweeps, and jubilee

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:43.707
migrate for one new column. A list of re-checks in the admin application

00:02:43.707 --> 00:02:45.050
is not built yet.
